    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **52 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist for `POST /api/owners`.\n\nThe email is already validated and normalized in `ValidateOwnerFields` (the first pipeline step, which rejects invalid fields with a 400 via `OwnerFieldsInvalidException`), so that's the natural place for the check. In `ValidateOwnerFields.java` I:\n\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n- After the existing syntax check and lower-casing, extracted the domain (portion after the final `@`) and threw `OwnerFieldsInvalidException(List.of(\"email\"))` \u2014 a 400 \u2014 when it's on the blocklist.\n\nComparison is done on the lower-cased email so mixed-case domains are caught too, and the rule keeps email optional (absent/blank emails are untouched).\n\nThe new `Cp38Tests.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes, and all 52 existing tests remain green.",
